---
import Inner from "../layouts/Inner.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <Inner>
    <p>
      This website was build with <a class="astro" href="https://astro.build/"
        >Astro</a
      >. Normally I use <a class="svelte" href="https://svelte.dev/">Svelte</a> to
      build highly interactive experiences. However when I don't need the interactivity
      that Svelte provides, I reach for Astro to hand-craft a small and performant
      static site.
    </p>
    <p>
      The background for this website is a large SVG made in Adobe Illustrator.
      It's animated entirely using CSS, allowing it work without JavaScript,
      while still loading extremely fast. Sadly, Astro transitions do not
      support persisting CSS animation state, so we need to manually save and
      set the state of every animation during navigation, and the result is not
      ideal.
    </p>
    <p class="reducedmotion mobile">
      The background moves! You're not seeing it because your system has
      prefers-reducted-motion turned on, or you're on a mobile device (for
      performance reasons the effect has been turned off).
      <button
        onclick="document.querySelector('#bg').classList.toggle('override')"
      >
        Override background movement
      </button>
    </p>
    <p>
      Fonts were optimized and subset, allowing me to still use the alternative
      R glyph for Roboto (which is missing in many versions of the font), while
      keeping the website slim.
    </p>
  </Inner>
</Layout>

<style>
  a.astro {
    color: #ad41ff;
  }
  a.svelte {
    color: #ff3e00;
  }
  .reducedmotion,
  .mobile {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion) {
    .reducedmotion {
      display: block;
    }
  }
  @media (min-height: 100vw) {
    .mobile {
      display: block;
    }
  }
</style>
